Backport of swoole/swoole-src commit 1e018553a ("Fix io_uring kernel version check to correctly
handle major version > 6", PR #6085), which landed on master and in the 6.3 line and was never
backported to 6.2.

Without it, a swoole built where the host kernel was 6.7 or newer aborts on a host kernel of 7.x:
`minor` is then 0, so `minor >= 7` is false and the guard reports a kernel too old to run what the
running kernel supports perfectly well. swoole_error() is fatal, so every process that constructs
an Iouring dies with:

    Iouring::Iouring(): The Iouring::futex_wait()/Iouring::futex_wakeup() requires `6.7` or higher Linux kernel

Whether the guard is compiled in at all is decided by config.m4 against the *build* host's kernel
(`test $KERNEL_MAJOR -eq 6`), so an image built on 6.x and run on 7.x is exactly the case that
breaks, and it is the case CI will be in the day its builders move to a 7.x kernel.

Drop this patch when the pinned swoole reaches 6.3, which carries the fix: `git apply` will fail
loudly on the version bump rather than let a stale patch pass unnoticed.

diff --git a/src/coroutine/iouring.cc b/src/coroutine/iouring.cc
--- a/src/coroutine/iouring.cc
+++ b/src/coroutine/iouring.cc
@@ -116,13 +116,13 @@
     parse_kernel_version(SwooleG.uname.release, &major, &minor);

 #ifdef HAVE_IOURING_FUTEX
-    if (!(major >= 6 && minor >= 7)) {
+    if (!((major > 6) || (major == 6 && minor >= 7))) {
         swoole_error("The Iouring::futex_wait()/Iouring::futex_wakeup() requires `6.7` or higher Linux kernel");
     }
 #endif

 #ifdef HAVE_IOURING_FTRUNCATE
-    if (!(major >= 6 && minor >= 9)) {
+    if (!((major > 6) || (major == 6 && minor >= 9))) {
         swoole_error("The Iouring::ftruncate() requires `6.9` or higher Linux kernel");
     }
 #endif
